WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:04.968
When a pod breaks at 2 a.m.,
the fastest command is delete.

2
00:00:04.968 --> 00:00:07.906
It's also the one that
destroys your evidence.

3
00:00:07.906 --> 00:00:11.099
kube-noob makes your AI
do it the other way round.

4
00:00:12.898 --> 00:00:15.942
Here is a Deployment
that works on a laptop.

5
00:00:15.942 --> 00:00:19.609
On OpenShift 4.22, kube-noob
scores it 37 out of 100.

6
00:00:19.609 --> 00:00:25.006
The password is hard-coded, the UID is
pinned, and privilege escalation is on.

7
00:00:25.006 --> 00:00:27.082
Every finding carries its fix,

8
00:00:27.082 --> 00:00:30.818
and the RHACS policy it would
trip where there is one.

9
00:00:30.818 --> 00:00:36.215
One command applies the safe fixes, and
it tells you what it left for a human.

10
00:00:38.015 --> 00:00:39.462
Now paste the events.

11
00:00:39.462 --> 00:00:42.975
Pods are rejected by a
security context constraint.

12
00:00:42.975 --> 00:00:48.142
kube-noob gives the cause, then read-only
steps first: get, describe, logs.

13
00:00:48.142 --> 00:00:51.174
Anything that runs in
a container or changes

14
00:00:51.174 --> 00:00:54.274
the cluster comes last
and asks for approval.

15
00:00:54.274 --> 00:00:55.790
The crash-looping pod?

16
00:00:55.790 --> 00:00:58.132
It's out of memory, exit code 137.

17
00:00:59.932 --> 00:01:06.052
Describe an app for ROSA HCP, and the
7-step protocol generates the Deployment,

18
00:01:06.052 --> 00:01:12.018
Route, PodDisruptionBudget, autoscaler
and NetworkPolicies, then audits them:

19
00:01:12.018 --> 00:01:13.180
100 out of 100.

20
00:01:14.980 --> 00:01:16.319
Learning Kubernetes?

21
00:01:16.319 --> 00:01:20.271
Lessons and exercises are graded
offline by the same rules.

22
00:01:30.338 --> 00:01:32.893
When your team confirms a fix, save it.

23
00:01:32.893 --> 00:01:37.807
Next time, search finds your team's
note next to the docs, with a citation.

24
00:01:37.807 --> 00:01:40.493
Secrets, logs and manifests are rejected.

25
00:01:45.770 --> 00:01:47.875
There's no AI inside kube-noob.

26
00:01:47.875 --> 00:01:50.455
Claude or Lightspeed does the talking;

27
00:01:50.455 --> 00:01:55.752
kube-noob supplies the rules and the
citations, or you use the CLI on its own.

28
00:01:55.752 --> 00:02:00.301
It makes no network calls and reads
no cluster unless you allow it,

29
00:02:00.301 --> 00:02:03.221
and doctor shows exactly
what it can reach.

30
00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:06.433
Don't trust me.

31
00:02:06.433 --> 00:02:13.684
Run the self-test: 63 real questions
across Kubernetes, Helm, OpenShift 4.22,

32
00:02:13.684 --> 00:02:15.473
ROSA HCP and RHACS.

33
00:02:17.523 --> 00:02:22.217
Install it with uv tool install
kube-noob, then run kube-noob demo.

34
00:02:22.217 --> 00:02:24.179
Get it at kube-noob dot com.
